**Key Findings

* The existing poster is effective at attracting attention and communicating a small number of key benefits
* Its simple visual hierarchy should influence the website design
* The current experience lacks sufficient information for users to understand the programme fully
* Users are told why they should consider Movement to Work, but not clearly what they will actually do
* The two-week programme structure needs to be clearly communicated
* The specific skills participants gain are currently unclear
* Transferable skills need to be explained using practical examples
* Users need more information about CV, interview and application support
* The current experience relies heavily on users speaking directly with a Work Coach to learn more
* A dedicated website would allow users to explore the programme independently
* Local employment opportunities and sectors should be made more visible
* Travel information should be considered when presenting employment opportunities
* Users need to understand the benefits of completing the full programme
* The certificate of participation should be presented as a tangible outcome
* Users need a clear understanding of what happens after programme completion
* Interactive features could make employability information easier and more engaging to understand
* The website should expand on the poster without losing its simplicity and visual clarity
